but the weakest cyclization encoding. rxn_006 does not conserve mass even with the stated NH3 release, and the later thioamide editing and hydrolysis sequence remains under-specified. The path is conceptually coherent, not chemically complete.', 'From the cyclic hub onward, rxn_007 and rxn_008 are strong and literature-aligned. The pathway then breaks at rxn_009 and rxn_010, which are not mass-conserving as encoded, and the last two steps still need explicit water accounting. This is a plausible fragment in concept but not yet a valid one in stoichiometric detail.', 'Starting from the ring-opened cyanohydrin avoids the cyclization issue, and rxn_008 is sound. However, rxn_009, rxn_010, rxn_011, and rxn_012 are all unbalanced as encoded, so this fragment remains only conceptually valid. The environmental framing is fine; the problem is missing stoichiometric detail.', 'All three encoded steps in this terminal fragment have conservation issues. The intended chemistry matches the Patel network, but rxn_010 needs explicit H2O and likely H2S/byproducts, rxn_011 should eject H2O, and rxn_012 should consume 2 H2O. As written, this is not a valid stoichiometric path to arginine.', 'This is the least flawed listed fragment. The amination and nitrile hydrolysis are both chemically sensible and literature-supported, but rxn_011 is missing H2O as a product and rxn_012 is missing 2 H2O as reactants. Once those stoichiometric fixes are made, this should be a plausible terminal conversion to racemic arginine.']\n\n============================================================\nAddress the above issues in your new network. Do NOT repeat the same mistakes.\n", "raw_response": "{\n  \"target_molecule\": \"Arginine\",\n  \"overall_strategy\": \"The supplied literature strongly supports an all-surface cyanosulfidic route, so this network stays in evaporitic/geothermal surface pools rather than adding unsupported hydrothermal or biochemical detours. To preserve the requested 8-15 molecule