m cited studies?\n- Are literature citations present in reaction reasoning?\n- Does the network acknowledge critiques and known challenges identified in the research?\n- Departures from the research are acceptable when explicitly and soundly justified.\n\n## Scoring Guidelines\n- 0.9-1.0: Excellent network, valid and chemically sound\n- 0.8-0.9: Good network with minor issues\n- 0.7-0.8: Acceptable but with notable concerns\n- 0.5-0.7: Significant problems with validity or chemistry\n- 0.0-0.5: Major issues, network is not viable\n\nA network is APPROVED if overall_confidence >= 0.9\n\nOutput your evaluation as JSON matching the NetworkEvaluation schema.\n", "user_message": "Evaluate this synthesis network:\n\nTARGET MOLECULE: Arginine\nOVERALL STRATEGY: The supplied literature strongly supports an all-surface cyanosulfidic route, so this network stays in evaporitic/geothermal surface pools rather than adding unsupported hydrothermal or biochemical detours. To preserve the requested 8-15 molecule scope while retaining the chemistry unique to arginine, the graph begins at 3-aminopropanenitrile, the immediate precursor made upstream in the broader Patel et al. cyanosulfidic system. Cyanamide installs the guanidino functionality, three literature-inspired Cu/H2S cyclization condition variants converge on the same cyclic hemiaminal hub, HCN ring opening and sulfide/thioamide editing remodel the chain, and ammonolysis plus aqueous nitrile hydrolysis deliver racemic arginine.\n\nMOLECULES (15 nodes):\n  - mol_001: C3H6N2 (beta-aminopropionitrile) [starting]\n  - mol_002: CH2N2 (cyanamide) [starting]\n  - mol_003: HCN (hydrogen cyanide) [starting]\n  - mol_004: NH3 (ammonia) [starting]\n  - mol_005: H2S (hydrogen sulfide) [starting]\n  - mol_006: H2O (water) [starting]\n  - mol_007: S (elemental sulfur) [intermediate]\n  - mol_008: C4H8N4 (cyanoethylguanidine) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_009: C4H9N3O (cyclic guanidine hemiaminal) [hub_intermediate]\n  - mol_010: C5H10N4O (